After finishing my first game, I now start experimenting mode eg. try to
experiment as much as possible.
In this stage (Im sure many feels like me) one tries another caracter (race)
for a new quest, but its not as fun as the first win-game.

Some tries I will do is about my little pet. Some questions about him:

1. Will he follow through magic portals?
2. If I leash him, what if I levitate over water?
3. If he eats a red dragon, will he be fire resistant?
4. If I leash him and level teleport, will he follow/die?
5. If a monster eats him, will he be digested immidiately or can I pull
   him out?

I have more questions that I will try, but this is enough for the moment.
I think that the pet should have a larger part of this game than it has
today. Imagine one has a dog who saves one's life several times then just
dump him, and later kill him! Sad story which should make the gods ANGRY!!!

There should be a way to bring the pet to the endgame!

I dont feel to strong about this suggestion, but I always found it VERY
satisfying during my NH1.0 days when I escaped together with my pet and
read in the highscorelist
Escaped dungeon with amulet and a dog (or a shopkeeper)!!!
(Once I had three mad shopkeepers who followed me out of the dungeon. It
was hard to get them all in position around me at the upstairs, but it was 
possible with some work.)

